#X msg 110 493 @mode;
#X text 245 493 Get/Set output mode. 'full' - output the convolution
at each point of overlap \, with an output length of (M+N-1). At the
end-points of the convolution \, the signals do not overlap completely
\, and boundary effects may be seen. 'valid' - output of length (max(M
\, N)-min(M \, N)+1). The convolution product is only given for points
where the signals overlap completely. Values outside the signal boundary
have no effect. 'same' - output of length max(M \, N). Boundary effects
are still visible. Type: symbol. Default value: full. Allowed values:
valid \, same \, full.;
